youtube.description:
Most small businesses don't have a lead problem, they have a leak. A form submitted on Tuesday night gets seen on Thursday, and by then someone else has answered. In this video we build the fix in n8n, step by step from an empty canvas, and then run it live: a real form, a real inbox, a real phone.

WHAT WE BUILD
Lead catcher: On form submission → Tidy lead (Edit Fields) → Save lead (Google Sheets, Append or Update Row, matched on email) → Reply to lead (Gmail) → Alert me (Telegram) → Wait until next working morning → Look up lead (Google Sheets, Get Row(s)) → Still new? (If) → Remind me (Telegram).
Lead alarm: Error Trigger → Telegram, set as Lead catcher's error workflow.

SHEET HEADERS (row 1)
received_at | name | email | phone | need | source | status | replied_at

EXPRESSIONS
name: {{ $json.Name.trim() }}
email: {{ $json.Email.trim().toLowerCase() }}
received_at: {{ $now.toFormat('yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm') }}
Gmail To: {{ $('Tidy lead').item.json.email }}
Wait (At Specified Time): {{ $now.plus({ days: $now.weekday >= 5 ? 8 - $now.weekday : 1 }).set({ hour: 9, minute: 0, second: 0, millisecond: 0 }).toISO() }}
Look up filter: email = {{ $('Tidy lead').item.json.email }}
Still new?: {{ $json.status }} is equal to new
Telegram chat ID: message your bot, then open https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates and copy result → message → chat → id

SELF-HOSTED NOTES
Google: create an OAuth client (Web application) in Google Cloud, enable the Sheets, Drive and Gmail APIs, and use the OAuth redirect URL n8n shows you. Publish the consent screen once it works, or the sign-in expires after 7 days in testing mode.
Set WEBHOOK_URL to your real domain so the form's production URL isn't localhost, and set GENERIC_TIMEZONE (or the workflow's timezone) so 9 am means your 9 am.
Error workflows only run for live executions, not manual tests.
